error[DS0115]: `where` takes one condition
  --> query:1:17
  |
1 | from t | where a, b;
  |                 ^ a comma does not join conditions
  |
  = help: combine the conditions with `and`: `a and b`

error[DS0101]: expected `|` or `;`, found `,`
  --> query:2:17
  |
2 | from t | where a,;
  |                 ^

error[DS0101]: expected `|` or `;`, found `,`
  --> query:3:30
  |
3 | from t | top 5 by amount desc,;
  |                              ^

error[DS0101]: expected `|` or `;`, found `,`
  --> query:4:16
  |
4 | from t | take 5,;
  |                ^

error[DS0101]: expected `)`, found `,`
  --> query:5:34
  |
5 | from t | where a between (1 .. 10,);
  |                          -       ^
  |                          |
  |                          to close this `(`

error[DS0101]: expected `)`, found `,`
  --> query:6:23
  |
6 | from t | extend x = (a,);
  |                     - ^
  |                     |
  |                     to close this `(`

error[DS0101]: expected `]`, found `,`
  --> query:7:24
  |
7 | from t | extend x = a[0,];
  |                      - ^
  |                      |
  |                      to close this `[`

error[DS0116]: `distinct *` cannot list other columns
  --> query:8:19
  |
8 | from t | distinct *,;
  |                   ^ `*` already means every column
  |
  = help: remove `*` to keep the distinct values of the listed columns, or remove the columns to keep distinct rows

error[DS0101]: expected `)`, found `,`
  --> query:9:30
  |
9 | from t | extend x = long(null,)
  |                         -    ^
  |                         |
  |                         to close this `(`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from t | where a and b;
    from t | where a,;
    from t | top 5 by amount desc,;
    from t | take 5,;
    from t | where a between (1 .. 10,);
    from t | extend x = (a,);
    from t | extend x = a[0,];
    from t | distinct *,;
    from t | extend x = long(null,)
